 stem:"A patient with osteoarthritis has been taking steroids for a long time. One day the patient felt unwell and had to take antibiotics, so the usual medication was stopped. The patient then developed abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting. Vital signs: BP 90/60 mmHg, PR 110/min, RR 24/min. What is the diagnosis?",
